                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_467">Robertsbridge, Sussex.
                        Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>The manuscript has long
                        been associated with NLW MS 13210D (which contains an inscription for the
                        abbey) and Princeton UL MS 159. The books were still together during John
                        Parker's time, when they were listed as one volume, but had been separated
                        into discrete bindings by the time of their sale to Thomas Phillipps in
                        1828.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Matthew Parker (1504–1575), archbishop of
                     Canterbury.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John Parker (1548–1619), son of the
                     archbishop; pawned by his son Richard.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Richard Stanley, grandson of William Stanley,
                     master of Corpus Christi College, Cambridge from 1693–8, by whom sold at
                     Christie's, 10 March 1828, to:</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir Thomas Phillipps, baronet (1792–1872),
                     collector.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Phillipps sale, Sotheby's, 25 November 1969,
                     lot 455, to William Dawson &amp; Sons. Now untraced.</provenance>
               </history>
